error[E0315]: a macro can't have type parameters
  --> tests/ui/macro_decl_errors.wid:12:22
   |
12 | macro def generic(x: $T) -> Code
   |                      ^^ a `$` type parameter
   = note: a macro runs once per call, while compiling; it receives types as values
help: take the type as a `Type` parameter, like `t: Type`, and splice it where a type goes with `#{t}`; take the value as `Code`
